he bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $32K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Biglari Holdings Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $1.2B market cap on $395M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at -1% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $77M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 19 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -4.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (16.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 17% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 49% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.4919951315419906},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Consumer Cyclical peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Large open-market insider purchases (net $11.1M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Among the least levered in Consumer Cyclical \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Biglari GAAP EPS of -$3.91, revenue of $112.1M (NYSE:BH.A)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4668627-biglari-gaap-eps-of-3_91-revenue-of-112_1m","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794000662.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"BIGLARI HOLDINGS INC. NEWS RELEASE","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/biglari-holdings-inc-news-release-302932416.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794000360.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Biglari Holdings (BH.A) Could Be 35% Above Fair Value Following A Sharp Pullback","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-services/nyse-bh.a/biglari-holdings/news/biglari-holdings-bha-could-be-35-above-fair-value-followi